fact WorkItem(id: "WI-679", description: some(value: "lf1 transponder ranking proof: derive decrease_violation_transponder / bound_violation_transponder's upc transition from the step operation body via WI-669 defining-equation extraction, retiring the hand-written restatement.\n\nFIRST STEP (inline, not a separate prereq): add Expr::Let handling to kb/body_specialize.rs::reduce — today it hard-declines let (catch-all _ => None), and step's body is let-heavy (let new_delta / new_yaw_cmd / new_upc / new_seq). The let arm mirrors reduce_match's Env extension: reduce the bound expr, extend the existing Env (the operational face of proposal-050 Gamma's binding component), reduce the continuation; reuse shadow / collect_bound_names. Scope = simple non-destructuring 'let name = expr' (step uses only that); escalate let to its OWN ticket ONLY if destructuring-lets or ANF flattening of nested BODIED-op calls is needed (step's nested calls are arithmetic operators, no self-recursion, so neither expected). Also needs match support (step matches on Option prev_distance/prev_delta) — WI-669 inc-1a declines a residual match; either the scrutinees resolve concretely or add ADT-match defining equations.\n\nTHEN: defining_equations(step) yields the upc-update as an ite-chain over inputs; the ranking proof references step(...).upc instead of the hand-written ?upc_next = ?upc + 1. Field access .upc already works (WI-482).\n\nDRIFT TO CONFIRM/RESOLVE: the hand-written ?upc_next = ?upc + 1 appears to DIVERGE from step's clamp-through-0 (else if gte(state.upc,0) then state.upc+1 else 0): for post-armed upc < 0 the body yields new_upc = 0 (snap to 0), NOT upc+1. If confirmed at runtime, deriving from the body changes the obligation and may revise the N=6 PostArmedExcursionBound. This drift is EXACTLY what WI-669 body-derivation removes. (Comment/code mismatch at follower_transponder.anthill:62-64 'incremented while shrinking faster' vs code decrements — separate readability note.)\n\nACCEPTANCE: the transponder ranking proof (proof post_armed_excursion_bound) discharges from step-body-derived defining equations with NO hand-written upc-transition rule body; discharge.sh + anthill check green (or N corrected if the drift is real, justified from the body); cargo-test green.\n\nDEPENDS: WI-669 (defining-equation engine + SMT seam). Second lf1 consumer alongside WI-681 (GPS desired_position); this is the LIA/integer-state-machine case, WI-681 the QF_NRA geometry case."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-669"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-11T14:36:49Z"))
